This is just a wild guess.
I have heard that there can be problems when the system has that
type of ehternet card installed that has redundancy via a switch.
(on the DEC system)

Apparently, the two interfaces on the same card send heart beats
to each other. If there are connected via a switch the switch
gets confused (something to do with the MAC address or
something) and performance degrades.

Solution is to not to use a switch but a HUB or to disconnect
one of the interfaces.

I hope this helps

