Steven Colligan <s.colligan@tay.ac.uk> wrote:
: We have an ageing AlphaServer 2000 with Digital Unix 3.2B on it (okay I know
: it's long out of date but it's a system that is being retired later this
: year).

: My current problem is that when booting, it reports that it can't open the
: osf_boot file.  Is there anyway to restore this file from say a bootable
: floppy or CD.

: Has this happened to anyone else and what did you do to get by this
: predicament?

I have once seen a similar syndrome. The machine was booting
from AdvFS, but the sysadmin (not I) had created a UFS file system
on the same disk. By mistake he had done it in a way that made
the machine think it was booting from UFS. The solution was to
boot the machine from CD, and then write a correct label
to the disk. The correct disklabel command can be found
in the AdvFS manual, in the section that describes how
to migrate the system disk from UFS to AdvFS.

