luciano_zz@libero.it wrote:

> I have an acoount on an aplha running tru64 digital unix V4.0 with
> apache.
> Where should I  put my html file in order to have my own web page ?
> How can I do this ?

Check with the sysadmin for that machine.  Usually you create a
public_html or WWW directory in your account and put your web files in
that.  The directory name that the web server looks for is configured in
the web server conf files:  probably httpd.conf.

Once you have the directory name, just create it and make sure that your
home directory and the web directory has at least execute privileges
given to the world and that your web files are readable to the world.

Steve

