	You're not asking your question clearly enough.  Do you mean that
each machine is configured standalone with its own "/etc/passwd"
file and only certain users are in each machine's password file?  If
that is your problem all you have to do is start running NIS.  Make
one machine the master and put everyone's password file entry on
it.  Make another machine a slave NIS server so that you have some
redundancy.  Make all the rest clients.  Use "nissetup" to do it. 
The next step would be to move all the home accounts to a central
server and use the automounter to serve the files.  Then you can do
nightly backups on that one server.

			Hope this helps,
			      Don


