> I'm a Linux guy now working in a shop that uses Digital Unix v4.
> I'm looking for a way to go back commands like under Linux using the up
> and down keys. Is there a way to do this with OSF? Using what shell?

I believe the standard csh on DU is now based on tcsh, which recognizes
up and down arrows; if not then you can get and use tsch.  You can also
switch to ksh which offers both vi and emacs style editting on any real
ksh on nay platform.  Make sure you have history turned on or there
won't be anything to recall in ksh.

You're probably using bash on Linux, bash shoudl run fine on DU.

