mkfdmn /dev/rz3h test_domain
mkfset test_domain test

mount -t advfs test_domain#test /test

and add it in the file fstab
you can reconfigure the disk with the cmd
disklabel -rwn /dev/rz3h rzxx (rzxx if you dont know
the type of your disk)
I you want to create a root domain
