With DU 4.x, this wouldn't happen in my experience.  Discovered
when using OpenBSD as an NFS client.  OBSD would check that
source address was as expected on incoming packets and quietly
drop them if they didn't match.  Using the cluster alias in the
client config would result in responses with an actual address.
Result was that physical machine addresses had to be used and
so any failover/load balancing effect sought was negated.

Asked the devs if/when this would be changed and never had a
response.  Of course, deciding whether or not to rewrite the
source address on a packet could be a nasty bit of logic.

