I run a 4 CPU/8GB GS140 on 4.0f without problems attributed with DUnix.
I think you'll find that your crashes will be realted to 3rd party kernel
add-ins (like ADIC's AMASS, which I use) or misconfigured drivers.

GS140 hardware is very robust and the ROM monitor diags will catch things
that the resident OS may never tickle (like marginal banks of memory).

You are running this unit off of an on-line UPS, right? Even considering the
hardness of the native PS modules in the GS140/8400, all sorts of problems
occur on 3-phase power lines that you would normally not see on 1-phase
lines.






