Currently I use the following command on our Digital Alphastation 4/166's
(with OSF/1) to obtain a listing of subdirectories without the associated
clutter of file names:

ls -p | grep "/"

This command uses "-p" to place a "/" at the end of each directory name,
(but not file names), then searches for and displays only those entries with
a "/", yielding a display of only the subdirectories. I do this because the
directory has about 50,000 files in it and I have no other brief method of
displaying just the directory names.

QUESTION:  IS THERE A BETTER WAY? Is there an "ls" option that does this?


Mark M.





