We have had two DEC Alphastation 4/166 machines for a number of years,
running OSF/1. They are very stable. Our only complaint would be that they
are not nearly as stable as DEC VMS for when you intentionally or
unintentionally crash a machine. VMS never fails in these situations. We've
had VMS crash many times over the years on many different DEC machines.
There is never a problem rebooting. But when the Alphastations crash due to
a power-off/on you will occasionally get a media error on the disk and not
be able to reboot.

We have a site that operates Process Control software on these two identical
Alphastations 24 hours a day. Electricians will come power off/on the
machines when there is a problem with the Process Control software. They do
not do an orderly shutdown. They just pull the plug on everything! You can't
convince them to do otherwise, nor do you want to at 2:00am.

For this reason I say that OSF/1 is not as robust as VMS, but otherwise
appears to be robust.

Mark M.




