Arnaud LHUILLIER wrote:
> 
> edit or create a file /etc/inet.local
> in this file insert
> ifconfig tu0 alias 192.168.1.10 netmask 255.255.255.0
> I suppose tu0 is you interface
> 

Actually, on Digital Unix / OSF1 / Tru64 the correct file to edit is
/etc/rc.config. Increase the value of MAX_NETDEVS to 2 (or however many
aliases you want). Change the entry for NETDEV_1 (and NETDEV_2, etc. if
needed) to tu0 (or whatever is used for NETDEV_0). Finally, change the
value for IFCONFIG_1 to "alias 192.168.4.2 netmask 255.255.255.0". When
you reboot next, use "ifconfig -a" to verify that everything is
configured as expected.


