Brandon Lovelace wrote:
> 
> Hello all,
>     I am having the damdest time getting a  tape device (mkb0) on our second
> SCSI card (pkb0) to do a backup using vdump under 4.0D, Alpha Server 800
> 5/333 fwv 5.5...  Here's what happens...
> 
> $ vdump -0 -f /dev/nrmt10h /home/student
> vdump: can't open dev </dev/nrmt10h>; [6] No such device or address
> 
> Now /dev/nrmt10h is under the /dev directory, and I believe that to be the
> proper device (I've tried nrmt0h, no luck).  So I guess my question is, what
> in the heck am I doing wrong?  Do I need to run the MAKEDEV script again,
> and if so what are the proper arguments to get the tape working correctly?
> Anyway if anyone knows how to fix this I would much appreciate it...

A couple of things you could do :

Do a "scu show edt" to see what SCSI devices unix can see.
Grep for tz in /var/adm/messages to see if the tape drive is seen at
boot time and what name it has.
Do a "file /dev/nrmt?h". It should return a string stating what type of
device, what SCSI ID and so on if the device file is OK and the device
is on(line).
Make a new device file with "./MAKEDEV tz*". You can replace * with the
number from /var/adm/messages.


l8r/Jspr



