You have the wrong idea about Samba. Others will give you more
technical descriptions but, in essence, Samba emulates PC sharing of
filesystems and printers on a UNIX system - it is not installed on PCs.
To a PC the UNIX system running Samba looks like another PC with shares
it can access. We have used it for years over TCP/IP as the standard
method of allowing PC users access to their home directories, special
filesystems and printers on UNIX  servers. 
